# Backend Rules

## Allowed

- `AppError` hierarchy for typed errors
- `createAction()` wrapper for Server Actions
- `createRouteHandler()` wrapper for Route Handlers
- `ActionResult<T>` return type (shared by actions and API routes)
- `logger` for structured logging
- `import "server-only"` in server modules
- Zod validation before service calls
- Rate limiting in Route Handlers only (not in domain services)

## Forbidden

- Throwing raw errors across action/route boundaries
- `console.log` in production code
- Silent catch blocks
- Business logic in `src/server/` (only cross-cutting infra)
- Business logic in Route Handlers (`src/app/api/`)
- Exposing stack traces or SQL errors to clients
- Trusting client-supplied prices or entity IDs

## Error types

- `ValidationError` (400) — Zod/input failures
- `NotFoundError` (404) — missing resources
- `DomainRuleError` (422) — business rule violations
- `ConflictError` (409) — idempotency key mismatch
- `UnauthorizedError` (401) — auth failures
- `InfrastructureError` (500) — internal, not exposed

## Route Handler pattern

```typescript
// src/app/api/reservations/route.ts
export const POST = createRouteHandler({
  schema: createReservationInputSchema,
  rateLimit: { limiter, policy, buildBucketKey },
  handler: async (input, request) => {
    // delegate to service only — no business rules here
    return bookingService.createReservation(input, { idempotencyKey });
  },
});
```

## Service pattern

```typescript
// features/booking/server/service.ts
export class BookingService {
  constructor(
    private readonly repository: BookingWriter,
    private readonly quoteService: QuoteService,
  ) {}
  // domain behavior here
}
```
